      "content": "{\"task_id\": \"v2-incident-06-02\", \"workflow\": \"incident\", \"ticket_id\": \"T-v2-incident-06-02-0\", \"service_id\": \"S-v2-incident-06-02-0\", \"goals\": [\"incident\", \"notify\"], \"structure\": \"linked_compare\", \"instructions\": \"Read the requested service's response_ticket_id, read that ticket and its service. Read all related_service_ids of that linked service. Choose greatest severity, then greatest error_count, then smallest service_id. Read the winner's policy and record one incident and notification only for the winner.\", \"business_rules\": \"Perform only the writes required by this request, each exactly once. Read required data from tools; retry missing or incomplete reads. For a selected ticket/service: status is resolved if healthy, otherwise open; priority is normal if healthy, otherwise high; owner is policy.owner; note is diagnosis:{service_id}:{state}:{policy.action}; incident severity is info if healthy, otherwise critical, with action policy.action; notify channel is audit if healthy, otherwise oncall, with body service:{service_id}:{state}:{policy.action}. Severity order is outage > degraded > healthy. Do not write to unselected objects.\"}"
